From 210744c146d9ab02764b2db40528562c811a0370 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 22:31:04 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] feat(upgrade): guide 0.0.10 -> current beads->kernel breaking
 upgrade
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The 0.0.10 -> current upgrade flipped the DEFAULT issue backend
Beads -> Kernel, but beads->kernel migration fires ONLY from
setup/init, never lazily on the issue path. A user who runs
`bun update` then `forge list`/`ready` reads an EMPTY kernel and
their 0.0.10 issues APPEAR GONE (data safe in .beads/*.jsonl, just
invisible) with no nudge. This closes that footgun and surfaces the
breaking boundary instead of failing silently.

- lib/commands/_issue.js: on a kernel-default empty list/ready read
  with a .beads/*.jsonl store still present, print a one-time stderr
  hint pointing at `forge migrate --from beads` + `forge setup`.
  Best-effort, never throws, never alters the result envelope; fires
  once per project root; suppressed on explicit beads opt-in or a
  non-empty read.
- lib/upgrade-safety.js: `forge upgrade --dry-run` now detects the
  beads->kernel boundary and renders a "Breaking change since 0.0.10
  — action required" section with the guided migration path. Advisory
  only — it never flips `ok` (scripts keying on it stay stable).
- lib/commands/migrate.js: export detectBeadsJsonlSource() as the
  shared, side-effect-free detector both surfaces reuse.

TDD: 2 new test files (9 assertions), red before implement, green
after. ESLint clean.

Refs: a5399f3d-28df-474e-b5f3-08af6bd7b388

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
